# A Killer Among Us: only a token of the chosen type gets the bonuses ("if target attacking creature token is the chosen type").
# Bot1 chose Human but targets the attacking Goblin token: the cost is paid (the enchantment is sacrificed, Human revealed), and on
# resolution the Goblin is not a Human, so it gets no counters and no deathtouch; the ability does nothing else (CR 608.2b).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
A Killer Among Us
Forest x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.A Killer Among Us.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Human)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Goblin Token > Bot2)
Bot1.Battlefield.A Killer Among Us.Activate(Target: Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Token)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.A Killer Among Us = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Token.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Token.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Token.Keywords = (absent)
Bot2.Life = 19
